          <a href="#daytrips" class="px-4 py-2 bg-cyan-50 text-cyan-700 rounded-lg hover:bg-cyan-100 transition-colors font-medium text-sm">
            🚗 Farther Day Trips
          </a>
          <a href="#all" class="px-4 py-2 bg-purple-50 text-purple-700 rounded-lg hover:bg-purple-100 transition-colors font-medium text-sm">
            📍 All {nearbyHikes.length} Trails
          </a>
        </div>
      </div>

      <!-- Intro Content -->
      <div class="prose prose-lg max-w-4xl mx-auto mb-16 bg-white rounded-2xl p-8 shadow-sm border border-stone-200">
        <h2 class="text-3xl font-bold text-stone-900 mb-4">From Delaware's State High Point to the Kittatinny Ridge</h2>

        <p class="text-stone-700 leading-relaxed">
          Philadelphia doesn't sit near dramatic peaks, but real elevation is closer than it looks. Head
          south into Delaware's Piedmont and you'll find Ebright Azimuth — at 449 feet, the lowest state
          high point in the country, and a genuine hiking curiosity under an hour from Center City. Push
          north instead and the land rises through the Kittatinny Ridge and the New Jersey Highlands,
          culminating in Mount Tammany's cliff-edge views over the Delaware Water Gap.
        </p>

        <p class="text-stone-700 leading-relaxed">
          This guide covers all {nearbyHikes.length} trails within 100 miles of Philadelphia, sorted by
          actual distance from real trailhead coordinates — not the city center. Each trail includes:
        </p>

        <ul class="space-y-2 text-stone-700">
          <li>✓ <strong>Exact distance from Philadelphia</strong> (measured from the trailhead, not the summit)</li>
          <li>✓ <strong>Trail difficulty rating</strong> (easy, moderate, hard)</li>
          <li>✓ <strong>Elevation gain & distance</strong></li>
          <li>✓ <strong>Parking information & fees</strong></li>
          <li>✓ <strong>Interactive trail maps</strong></li>
          <li>✓ <strong>Real-time weather conditions</strong></li>
        </ul>
      </div>

      <!-- Closest Hikes Section -->
      {closestHikes.length > 0 && (
        <section id="closest" class="mb-16">
